# Index: Testing

Purpose:
  Testing knowledge base entry point. This directory defines HOW tests
  are written, executed, and evaluated across the whole system. Testing
  is split into two layers:
    - .sdd/testing/ defines reusable testing knowledge (types,
      levels, gates, principles) and execution scripts
    - .sdd/projects/{project_name}/testing/ tracks concrete project test state (coverage,
      runs, failures, exceptions)

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
  1  INDEX.sdd (this file)
  2  levels.sdd (test depth levels L0-L5)
  3  t-levels.sdd (test type levels T0-T7)
  4  types.sdd (test type definitions)
  5  gates.sdd (test gate criteria)
  6  bdd.sdd (BDD testing)
  7  unit.sdd (unit testing)
  8  integration.sdd (integration testing)
  9  api.sdd (API testing)
  10 contract.sdd (contract testing)
  11 e2e.sdd (end-to-end testing)
  12 ui.sdd (UI testing)
  13 mobile.sdd (mobile testing)
  14 performance.sdd (performance testing)
  15 load.sdd (load testing)
  16 scripts/run.ps1 (test runner)
  17 skills/testing/SKILL-TEST-STRATEGY.sdd (test strategy)

Rules:
  [TEST1] AI MUST select test types based on task impact, risk, and
          stack — not all test types apply to every task.
  [TEST2] BDD is a first-class citizen — business behavior MUST be
          defined in BDD before implementation starts.
  [TEST3] Test source code MUST NOT be mixed with .sdd metadata —
          source code stays in project test directories, .sdd stores
          only metadata and workflow.
  [TEST4] Test failures MUST create findings and feed back into the
          task graph (bax projects/{project_name}/testing/failures/).
  [TEST5] Test status MUST be tracked per task in projects/{project_name}/testing/.
  [TEST6] Flaky tests MUST be flagged separately from failures.
  [TEST7] Coverage is not just a percentage — critical path, risk, and
          mutation coverage MUST be considered.
  [TEST8] Test impact analysis MUST select only affected tests for a
          change — full regression is for merge/release only.
  [TEST9] Test gates MUST pass before a task can advance to DONE.
  [TEST10] Waived tests MUST have explicit approval and expiration.
  [TEST11] Test execution MUST be triggered from .sdd/testing/scripts/
          when AI runs tests, never from root-level test directories.

